  "ruling": "upheld",
  "reason": "The flag notes that 100% of the issue is an offer for sale, meaning all proceeds go to selling shareholders rather than the company. No RHP page among those provided (rhp:p42, p62, p63, p74, p245) discloses an ordinary explanation for the 100% OFS structure (e.g., that the company has no capital need, that the sale is to meet minimum public shareholding, or that promoters are providing liquidity). Without such disclosure, the elevated concern that the company receives no fresh capital remains.",
